    "final_text": "I added `updateQuantity(name, quantity)` to `ShoppingCart` in `src/cart.js`. The full suite passes with the 6 new tests (49 tests, 0 failures).\n\n- **Validation first:** a quantity that isn't a non-negative integer throws a `RangeError`. That includes negatives, `1.5`, `NaN`, `Infinity`, strings, `null` and `undefined`. `RangeError` is an `Error` subclass and matches the other cart methods.\n- **Missing item:** an item that isn't in the cart throws a plain `Error`. A quantity of 0 for a missing item also throws, since the item has to exist.\n- **Update:** a quantity of 0 removes the item, and any positive integer replaces its quantity.\n- **Rejected calls:** the cart is only modified after all checks pass, so a rejected call leaves it unchanged.\n\nThe new tests, in a new `updateQuantity` block in `tests/cart.test.js`, cover:\n- increasing and decreasing the quantity\n- removal at 0\n- negative and non-integer quantities\n- a missing item\n\nThe rejection tests also check the cart is unchanged afterwards.",
